                        "form": "ethnarques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c58dd6f8-949c-31d6-99bc-621850e1ce8e",
                        "entry_id": "db945210-d3c6-37c3-9ae6-c3681db59c41",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui règne sur, qui dirige un peuple."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6514dc0-5edc-464e-bace-89ba6ca35dc0",
                                "sense_id": "c58dd6f8-949c-31d6-99bc-621850e1ce8e",
                                "text": "L’hénothéisme proche-oriental (dieux ethnarques comme Yahweh, Marduk ou Qemosh) a abouti au monothéisme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ac161cd-7ff5-40fc-b724-b5fdc5ca902b",
                                "sense_id": "c58dd6f8-949c-31d6-99bc-621850e1ce8e",
                                "text": "Souvent proche des analyses d'Irénée qui s'oppose aux gnostiques, Cyrille critique la théorie des dieux ethnarques soutenue par Julien."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "891106db-1633-3064-b32f-a4a9457f1f0f",
                "word": "ethnarque",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "508ea080-add3-4ca5-b0b0-d194e3a7c147",
                        "entry_id": "891106db-1633-3064-b32f-a4a9457f1f0f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ethnarques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c78b264d-1c84-3c15-9d37-a12619722da0",
                        "entry_id": "891106db-1633-3064-b32f-a4a9457f1f0f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vassal de l'Empire romain qui commande un peuple sans se voir reconnaitre le titre de roi."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c98e6f75-593b-46f6-bdc0-804e1bc16c63",
                                "sense_id": "c78b264d-1c84-3c15-9d37-a12619722da0",
                                "text": "La communauté juive est dirigée par un ethnarque qui administre les affaires propres à ses coreligionnaires; il la représente auprès des instances royales et s'occupe de ses ordonnances."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26aef1de-bfff-496c-834c-7c1efcf7026b",
                                "sense_id": "c78b264d-1c84-3c15-9d37-a12619722da0",
                                "text": "En réalité, au 1ᵉʳ siècle après Jésus on ne note encore sur le territoire gaulois, que la présence de quelques judéens de marque, déportés en Gaule par ordre de l'autorité romaine et qui sont : L'ethnarque Archélaüs, fils d'Hérode, exilé en l'an 6 à Vienne et un autre fils d'Hérode."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c5bf1633-f134-370e-a180-e99b28c6ce35",
                        "entry_id": "891106db-1633-3064-b32f-a4a9457f1f0f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chef d'une troupe étrangère au service de l'empereur romain d'Orient."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5937600c-f3e9-4cb2-9348-0fd261fdc0bc",
                        "source_entry_id": "891106db-1633-3064-b32f-a4a9457f1f0f",
                        "target_lang_word": "ethnarch",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ethnarch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0385907b-16a0-343c-9e0f-bb5e9e54803c",
                                        "entry_id": "c6cd4586-c40e-3722-9202-f0cec984d12f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The governor of a Jewish province under the Roman Empire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb4d05da-f611-4f33-94b8-b13654d4a2e8",
                                                "sense_id": "0385907b-16a0-343c-9e0f-bb5e9e54803c",
                                                "text": "In the course of the struggle with the unfortunate ethnarch, the nobles had found it expedient to attach themselves to Rome."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9fb3e46e-e57f-33ac-94bc-fc591cbdc4f8",
                                        "entry_id": "c6cd4586-c40e-3722-9202-f0cec984d12f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A leader of an ethnic community, especially a Jewish or (in the Ottoman Empire) Eastern Orthodox leader having political as well as spiritual authority."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14f914e1-8048-4ed0-a43b-928aced82e10",
                                                "sense_id": "9fb3e46e-e57f-33ac-94bc-fc591cbdc4f8",
                                                "text": "In fact, from a worldly perspective, sages were petty clerks, employees of the ethnarch of their ethnic group. The ethnarch may have treated sages with […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38b05507-1bb6-4a50-a1dd-5b253e3a6356",
                                                "sense_id": "9fb3e46e-e57f-33ac-94bc-fc591cbdc4f8",
                                                "text": "The Archbishop became the ethnarch, the leader of the ethnic group. It was his responsibility to administer the territories where his people lived, to collect taxes and to regulate matters relating to marriage, divorce, dowry and inheritance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f028aa2c-ac75-40f6-bbf7-077c2d84de90",
                                                "sense_id": "9fb3e46e-e57f-33ac-94bc-fc591cbdc4f8",
                                                "text": "By the seventeenth century the archbishop became recognized as the ethnarch (ethnic political leader) of the Greek Cypriot community."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8aa80cc6-1329-409e-ae46-03eb27cb0586",
                                                "sense_id": "9fb3e46e-e57f-33ac-94bc-fc591cbdc4f8",
                                                "text": "But the Ethnarch, by tradition and long-established practice that had begun under the Ottomans, was more than a spiritual leader. He was expected to act as the spokesman, defender and protector of his flock."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9504e036-db13-4241-9984-91d0ffc99ee4",
